<title>INDIA: India forex reserves slip to $24.0 bln on Jan 3.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves slip to $24.0 bln on Jan 3.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves slipped to $24.0 billion on January 3, 1997 from $24.27 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Monday.  </p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					  Jan 3	 Dec 27	Jan 5</p>
<p>					   1997	  1996	  1996</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,748	19,802	 17,082</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,246	 4,347	  4,457</p>
<p>    SDRs				     6	   122	     18</p>
<p>    Total			     24,000	24,271	 21,557</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
